{
  "text": "2002B08 Outline the\npharmacological effects of vasopressin.\nList:\n·\nPC\n·\nPK\n·\nPD\nPharmaceutics: (not sure if\nwould score marks)\nStructure\n·\nNonapeptide\nProduction\n·\nSupraoptic and paraventricular hypothalamic\nnuclei\n(or synthetic)\nPharmacokinetics: (not sure if\nwould score marks)\nAdministration\n·\nHypotension: bolus 1-10 units, infusion 0.1-1\nunits/minute\n·\nArrest: bolus 40 units\nTime course\n·\nOnset <1 min\n·\nDuration 20-40 minutes for vascular effect,\nhours for renal effect\nAbsorption\n·\nMinimal (digested by peptidases)\nDistribution\n·\nPlasma protein binding 10-40%\nMetabolism\n·\nPeptidases in liver, kidneys; then\nrecycled\n·\nt\n1/2\nβ\n10-20\nminutes\nExcretion\n·\nSome renal excretion\nPharmacodynamics:\nMechanism of action\n·\nOxytocin receptor: G\nq\nG protein\ncoupled receptor\n·\n↑IP\n3\n/Ca\n2+\n,\n↑DAG\nV1\n·\nVascular smooth muscle\n·\nGeneralised vasoconstriction ->\n↑SVR > ↑PVR\nV2\n·\nLate distal tubule and collecting\nduct\no\nInsertion of aquaporin-2 into apical\nmembrane; endothelium\n·\nEndothelium\no\nRelease of vWF\nV3\n·\nAnterior pituitary\n·\n↑ACTH ->\n↑cortisol\nUse\n·\nCardiac arrest (alternative to\nadrenaline)\n·\n2\nnd\nline for vasoplegia (e.g. sepsis,\npost-cardiopulmonary bypass)\nSide effects\n·\nMild ↑PVR\n·\nOxytocin-like effects\nFeedback welcome at\nketaminenightmares@gmail.com",
